{
  "_comment": [
    "Target definition for compass/evaluate.py offline.",
    "",
    "Compass observations are free text. To score a prediction you need a",
    "finite target, so each dimension is reduced to ONE label from a fixed",
    "two-or-three-way vocabulary. The labels are the poles named in that",
    "dimension's own `description` field in dimensions.json - they are not",
    "invented for the metric and they are not tuned against the corpus.",
    "",
    "Reduction rule (compass/evaluate.py:reduce_label): lowercase the",
    "`observation` text (never `evidence` - that is a raw session quote and",
    "carries the user's words, not the claim), count case-insensitive",
    "substring hits for every cue of every label, take the argmax. Zero hits",
    "or a tie between the top two labels returns no label; those pairs are",
    "excluded from accuracy and reported as coverage/abstentions.",
    "",
    "Adding cues changes the metric. Do it before a measurement window, never",
    "in the middle of one, and never to make a number move."
  ],
